hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1405","Salam bin Junada, narrated to us by Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of his father, said: One of the princes sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about raindrops? Ibn Abbas said: What prevents him from asking me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out, humble, humble, humble, and supplicating. He prayed two rak’ahs as he prays on Eid, and he did not deliver a sermon. \"This is your engagement.\""
